  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_1",
  "label": "Transphobia is mapped onto the framed photo presentation",
  "description": "The top text 'no to transphobes' is juxtaposed with the visual of a group holding a framed photo of a trans woman. The framing of the photo, combined with the group's playful posing, creates an analogical mapping where the framed photo (a visual container) is mapped onto the concept of 'transphobia' as a social problem to be opposed. However, the visual metaphor of 'boxing in' the trans woman can be interpreted as mocking or ridiculing trans people, which is a form of transphobic stereotype. This mapping is implicit through the juxtaposition and the emotional tone conveyed by the visual material.",
